  fiber: 5 g
  sodium: 1711 mg
---

== Chicken ==

Blend the @lemon juice{2%tbsp}, @oregano{1%tbsp}(chopped), @ground coriander{1/2%tsp}, @garlic{3%cloves}(roughly chopped) and @light olive oil{1/4%cup} in a #blender{} until smooth. Season with @kosher salt{} and @ground black pepper{}.

Put the @chicken thighs{2%lb}(boneless, skinless, trimmed) in a 1-gallon #zip-top bag{} with half the marinade; refrigerate the other half. Marinate in the fridge ~{1%hour} to ~{4%hours}, turning the bag now and then.

Take the chicken out, pat it dry and season it with @kosher salt{} and plenty of @ground black pepper{}.

Heat the @vegetable oil{1%tbsp} in a 12-inch #heavy skillet{} over medium-high heat until it just smokes. Add the chicken and leave it alone ~{4%minutes}, until lightly browned underneath.

Turn the pieces, lower the heat to medium and cook ~{6%minutes} more, until the thickest part reads 165°F. Rest ~{5%minutes} on a board.

Chop into 1/4- to 1/2-inch pieces, toss with the reserved marinade in a bowl, cover and refrigerate while you make the rice and sauce.

== Rice ==

Melt the @unsalted butter{2%tbsp} in a #large Dutch oven{} over medium heat. Add the @turmeric{1/2%tsp} and @ground cumin{1/4%tsp} and stir ~{1%minute}, until fragrant but not browned.

Stir in the @long-grain rice{1 1/2%cup} and toast it, stirring often, ~{4%minutes}.

Add the @chicken broth{2 1/2%cup}, season with @kosher salt{} and @ground black pepper{}, and bring to the boil over high heat. Cover, turn down to a simmer and cook ~{15%minutes} without lifting the lid.

Take off the heat and leave covered ~{15%minutes}, until the liquid is absorbed and the rice is tender.

== White sauce ==

Whisk the @mayonnaise{1/2%cup}, @Greek yogurt{1/2%cup}, @sugar{1%tbsp}, @white vinegar{2%tbsp}, @lemon juice{1%tsp}, @parsley{1/4%cup}(chopped) and @ground black pepper{2%tsp} together. Season with @kosher salt{}.

== Assembly ==

Tip the chicken and all its juices back into the skillet and heat through over medium-high heat, stirring now and then.

Divide the rice, @iceberg lettuce{1%head}(shredded), @tomato{1}(large, in wedges) and @pita bread{}(buttered, toasted, cut in 1 by 3 inch strips) among the plates. Pile the chicken on the rice.

Spoon over the white sauce, add @hot sauce{}(harissa-style), and pass more sauce at the table.
